/** Standalone batch AA -- new 4-case standard (Sample + boundary + tricky + stress).
 * All solvers below were independently written and verified byte-for-byte against each problem's
 * real official Sample before being trusted to generate boundary/tricky/stress expected output,
 * EXCEPT uva-541 and uva-543 whose official Samples were both placeholders (see below).
 *
 * uva-514-rails: direct stack simulation -- push 1..N in increasing order, popping whenever the stack
 *   top matches the next needed target value; achievable iff this process consumes the entire target.
 *   Note: "2 3 1" (N=3) IS achievable this way (verified against the real sample) despite superficially
 *   resembling the classic 231 stack-sortability pattern -- "3 1 2" is the real sample's actual
 *   unsortable N=3 case, used for the tricky test instead.
 * uva-516-prime-land: reconstruct x from its prime-base (p,e) pairs, compute x-1, refactorize via
 *   trial division (x<=32767, so this is cheap), re-emit pairs in decreasing prime order. Verified
 *   against all 19 lines of the real sample, including several multi-prime-factor reconstructions.
 * uva-534-frogger: minimax-path Dijkstra variant (each relaxation minimizes the MAXIMUM edge weight
 *   along the path, not the sum) from stone 1 to stone 2, over the complete Euclidean-distance graph.
 * uva-536-tree-recovery: standard preorder+inorder recursive reconstruction (root = preorder[0], split
 *   inorder at the root's position, recurse left then right, emit root last for postorder).
 * uva-540-team-queue: O(1)-amortized team queue -- a queue of "which teams are currently present" plus
 *   a per-team FIFO of its own waiting members; ENQUEUE joins the team's own FIFO (and the team-order
 *   queue only if the team wasn't already present); DEQUEUE always pulls from the FRONT team's FIFO,
 *   retiring that team from the team-order queue once its FIFO drains.
 * uva-541-error-correction: THE SCRAPED OFFICIAL SAMPLE IS THE PLACEHOLDER "Please generate output by
 *   the sample code." -- not real data. Verified instead directly against the problem statement's own
 *   fully-illustrated 4x4 example (already-OK matrix), a single-bit flip of that same matrix (must
 *   name the exact (row,col) to fix), and a two-bad-row corruption (unfixable by any single change).
 *   sampleLimit: 0.
 * uva-543-goldbach-s-conjecture: THE SCRAPED OFFICIAL SAMPLE IS ALSO THE SAME PLACEHOLDER TEXT --
 *   sieve primes to 10^6 once, then for each n scan a=3,5,7,... ascending (the smallest valid a
 *   maximizes b-a since b=n-a shrinks as a grows) and take the first match. Verified directly against
 *   all three of the problem statement's own worked examples (8=3+5; 20's max pair 3+17 over 7+13;
 *   42's max pair 5+37 over the other three valid decompositions). sampleLimit: 0.
 */
import { seedFromSample } from "./testcase-seed-helper.js";

